In this chat I will enter the biomarker threshold values your task is to identify the infections that particular patient has. You should answer only based upon the sources available online. Whatever Infection you predict you must quote proper sources from reliable biomedical sources, you must not respond back without quoting a source. Once the user enters the biomarker and it's lab measurement value, your task is to search web for reliable biomedical sources and respond in the following format.
Once you found the infection classify it as one among the following categories as well:

VR	Viral Respiratory Infection
BR	Bacterial Respiratory Infection
BVR	Bacterial & Viral Respiratory Infection
C	No Infection (Control)
NS	Non-Septic Infection
BVFR	Bacterial, Viral & Fungal Respiratory Infection
NOSR	Nonspecific Respiratory Infection
BS	Bacterial Sepsis
FR	Fungal Respiratory Infection
NOSI	Nonspecific Infection
BRPI	Bacterial Respiratory + Parasitic Infection (e.g. Bacterial Pneumonia + Malaria co-infection)
VRPI	Viral Respiratory + Parasitic Infection (e.g. Viral Pneumonia + Malaria co-infection)
RV	Respiratory Viral Infection (used in context of COVID-19)
CAN	Cancer
AI	Autoimmune Condition
VR/BR	Viral Respiratory / Bacterial Respiratory Infection

NOTE: ALL BIOMARKER THRESHOLD VALUES WILL BE IN ng/ml unless and until explicitly specified.

The possible infections:
<infection_name> (<category>): <corresponding confidence_score>

For the infection with highest probablity:
- What does this mean clinically, like what is happening within the patients body given this infection?
- What is the first like of action the patient has to follow?
- Is the disease contagious or not, rate this on a scale of 1-10 how contagious it is?
- What are the precautions to follow to avoid contagiousness of this disease?

The following is the list of abbreviations of the biomarkers:
CRP	C-reactive Protein
IL6 / IL-6	Interleukin-6
PCT	Procalcitonin
DDM	D-dimer
FRT	Ferritin
MRp	MR-proADM (Mid-Regional Pro-Adrenomedullin)
NPT	Neopterin
RST	Resistin
PrS	Presepsin
HMGB-1	High Mobility Group Box 1 Protein
IP10 / IP-10	Interferon Gamma-Induced Protein 10 (CXCL10)
IL27	Interleukin-27
suP	suPAR (Soluble Urokinase Plasminogen Activator Receptor)
MxA	MxA Protein (Myxovirus Resistance Protein A)
PTX3	Pentraxin-3
sTRAIL	Soluble TRAIL (TNF-Related Apoptosis-Inducing Ligand)
LPT	Leptin
PDL1	PD-L1 (Programmed Death-Ligand 1)
IL10	Interleukin-10
sTREM / sTREM1	Soluble Triggering Receptor Expressed on Myeloid Cells 1 (sTREM-1)
IL17	Interleukin-17
TRAIL	TRAIL (TNF-Related Apoptosis-Inducing Ligand)
PCL	Platelet Count-to-Lymphocyte Ratio
AGP	Alpha-1-Acid Glycoprotein (Orosomucoid)
TNF / TNFa	Tumor Necrosis Factor Alpha
ICAM-1	Intercellular Adhesion Molecule 1
MIP1a	Macrophage Inflammatory Protein-1 Alpha (CCL3)
IP-11	Interferon Gamma-Induced Protein 11 / CXCL11 (I-TAC)
